KZ3 patch 2182 (RSX pass 158): per-key lock around the pipeline-library Load + create + Store (rsx_pl_lock.h).
ld_pl_create is reached from the preload workers, the template workers, the async compile workers and the walker, with
overlapping keys by design. Two threads missing the library for one key both compiled it and both called StorePipeline
(a Store of an existing name fails with E_INVALIDARG); a Load concurrent with the Store of that name has no defined
result. Load + create + Store now run under one of 64 stripe locks chosen by the key and the Load is re-run under the
lock, so a waiting thread gets the first thread's stored pipeline instead of compiling again. The lock is a leaf: only
D3D12 calls run inside it. New [pso-lib] line (per minute with the [pso-stat] line once the library was used, and at
shutdown): calls, lock-waits, second-thread-hits, loads/hits, creates, stores, store-rejects. Host test
tools/smoke/test_pl_lock.sh (threads, TSan, negative control).

